    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="aa7737fa-2c32-4ee2-8244-f4f6917dedc8">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the policy type as participating whole life, which directly aligns with the policy introduced in fact_sentence_1. This information supports and contextualizes the initial statement by specifying key characteristics of the insured product.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="29b4269d-f2dc-4371-857c-c53041540b11">
      <data key="d3">The classification of the policy as "participating whole life" defines the nature of the policy that has been assigned the specific policy number. This categorization contextualizes the purpose and benefits associated with the identified policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002">
      <data key="d3">The policy's status as participating whole life implies certain benefits like dividends and cash buildup, while the $250,000 face amount represents the guaranteed death benefit under this policy structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="bf1f70a7-46ad-4ace-b4cd-c595e8d81ca6">
      <data key="d3">The policy's classification as a participating whole life insurance plan implies certain financial benefits and structures, such as potential dividends and cash value growth. Knowing that David Chen is Margaret Rose Chen’s husband helps explain why he was designated as the primary beneficiary, aligning legal and familial relationships with the policy’s design.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="6798b2ae-9c41-40d4-a9ed-fcff5337565b">
      <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is participating whole life provides context for the nature of the contract, but it requires knowledge of the insured—Margaret Rose Chen—to fully identify who holds the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951">
      <data key="d3">The participating nature of the whole life policy enables flexible beneficiary arrangements, including contingent beneficiaries like the Chen Family Trust, ensuring the death benefit flows appropriately under specified conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is participating whole life explains why it accrues a cash surrender value over time due to its accumulation mechanism and dividend participation.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy is participating whole life, it accumulates cash value over time, enabling the availability of policy loans backed by that value.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy is a participating whole life insurance plan, it may allow conversion into Paid-Up Insurance, where the insured receives a lower death benefit but pays no more premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">converts to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7">
      <data key="d3">The statement about the policy being participating whole life provides context for why the premium payments extend until age 100, as such policies typically require lifetime premiums to maintain coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">consistent with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3">
      <data key="d3">The policy being classified as participating whole life indicates its capacity for dividends and long-term growth, while the specified annual premium of $3,240 reflects the recurring payment required to maintain that coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">Because the policy is participating whole life, it qualifies for potential dividend payments. These dividends represent returns of premiums and are determined annually by the insurer's board.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">The statement about the policy being participating whole life implies it builds cash value over time, making the definition of Cash Surrender Value meaningful within this context. This foundational characteristic enables the calculation described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53" target="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy is participating, it qualifies for dividends, which are directly influenced by the insurance company’s financial results and operating experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
