    </edge>
    <edge source="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002" target="6798b2ae-9c41-40d4-a9ed-fcff5337565b">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s $250,000 face amount applies specifically to Margaret Rose Chen, who is named as the insured, establishing that the coverage is directly linked to her life.</data>
      <data key="d4">associated with</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002" target="bf1f70a7-46ad-4ace-b4cd-c595e8d81ca6">
      <data key="d3">The policy's face amount of $250,000 establishes its death benefit value, which is relevant because it determines the payout upon Margaret’s passing. This ties into the naming of David Chen as the primary beneficiary due to his marital relationship with her.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual link</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002" target="696e047c-d749-4525-a7f2-29da3bb3dbc5">
      <data key="d3">The policy has a $250,000 face amount, which represents the death benefit payable to the designated primary beneficiary, David Chen, upon Margaret Rose Chen’s passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">payable to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002" target="f2b0d75b-5269-4ff2-968e-6b31adab60dd">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 face amount defines the total death benefit payable upon Margaret’s passing, ensuring David Chen receives exactly this sum as the designated primary beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002" target="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951">
      <data key="d3">The $250,000 face amount sets the total death benefit available, upon which the contingency plan for the Chen Family Trust relies when the primary beneficiary cannot receive the payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">The policy has a face amount of $250,000, which represents the maximum death benefit. This amount may be reduced if the policyholder chooses to convert to Paid-Up Insurance, where no further premiums are due but the death benefit decreases accordingly.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
