    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="aa7737fa-2c32-4ee2-8244-f4f6917dedc8">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s annual premium of $3,240 pertains specifically to the participating whole life insurance policy issued by Guardian Family Protection Corp.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">An annual premium of $3,240 supports a participating whole life policy, confirming the financial commitment needed to sustain a policy with dividend eligibility and cash accumulation features.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="6798b2ae-9c41-40d4-a9ed-fcff5337565b">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 is required to maintain the policy covering Margaret Rose Chen, ensuring continued protection and benefit accrual.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="d5e206b3-7b1d-4236-817f-e684a84db632">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 reflects the cost of coverage based on demographic factors such as age, which includes Margaret Rose Chen’s birthdate. Thus, the premium indirectly depends on her date of birth.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="3014bd72-c2ee-4fad-8aaa-dbdbec2cbc3e">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 reflects the underwriting assessment tied to Margaret's issue age of 45, making it consistent with standard pricing models.</data>
      <data key="d4">modified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="bedae073-61eb-409f-b92d-b26a51c1a904">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 reflects the financial cost associated with Margaret Rose Chen’s standard non-tobacco risk profile, indicating lower health-related risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="93e5c855-70f6-47b8-99fd-a2bc45122e25">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium amount of $3,240 implies regular yearly payments, consistent with the specified annual payment frequency.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="f2b0d75b-5269-4ff2-968e-6b31adab60dd">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 sustains the policy's validity, enabling future payouts such as the death benefit received by David Chen. Without consistent premium payments, the policy could lapse, preventing any payout regardless of beneficiary status.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 contributes to the accumulation of cash surrender value over time through policy growth and dividends. However, the definition of cash surrender value does not depend directly on the premium figure itself but rather on accumulated reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium contributes to building the cash value over time, which is a component used in calculating the cash surrender value after adjustments for loans and fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">The fixed annual premium establishes financial commitment, enabling future options like converting to Paid-Up Insurance, where no more premiums are needed despite a reduced payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 helps build the cash value over time, which enables future access to policy loans. Without sustained payments, the cash value would not accumulate sufficiently to support such loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The annual premium of $3,240 establishes the payment obligation under the policy, which forms part of the basis for potential future dividend distributions if the insurer declares them.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
