      <data key="d3">The annual payment frequency confirms that the $3,240 premium is due once per year, aligning with its designation as an annual premium.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="93e5c855-70f6-47b8-99fd-a2bc45122e25" target="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7">
      <data key="d3">Annual payment frequency means premiums are due once per year over the duration specified by the policy’s term, which ends at age 100.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="93e5c855-70f6-47b8-99fd-a2bc45122e25" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Annual premium payments enable the accumulation of cash value over time, which may allow conversion into Paid-Up Insurance later. This connection shows how consistent contributions support long-term policy flexibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="93e5c855-70f6-47b8-99fd-a2bc45122e25" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">Annual premium payments contribute to building cash surrender value over time, which enables future policy loans. Without sustained contributions like those specified annually, the accumulation of cash value would be delayed or insufficient.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
