    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="aa7737fa-2c32-4ee2-8244-f4f6917dedc8">
      <data key="d3">The extended premium payment period until age 100 indicates the policy’s longevity, supporting the classification of it as a whole life insurance product issued by Guardian Family Protection Corp.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">The extended premium payment period until age 100 is consistent with the characteristics of a participating whole life policy, where ongoing premiums support guaranteed benefits and potential dividends.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="d5e206b3-7b1d-4236-817f-e684a84db632">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums until age 100 relies on knowing Margaret’s current age, derived from her birthdate, to determine how long payments may continue.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="3014bd72-c2ee-4fad-8aaa-dbdbec2cbc3e">
      <data key="d3">The fact that the premium payment period continues until age 100 indicates lifelong financial obligations tied to the policy, which supports the inference that Margaret was likely underwritten at age 45, fitting typical actuarial assumptions for such policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">implies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="93e5c855-70f6-47b8-99fd-a2bc45122e25">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums until age 100 necessitates regular payments, consistent with the stated annual payment frequency.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">The extended premium payment period until age 100 ensures sustained funding for the policy, enabling accumulation of cash value over decades. This growing cash value serves as collateral for future policy loans, such as those offered under the terms described.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay the annual premium of $3,240 persists throughout the policyholder’s life until she turns 100.</data>
      <data key="d4">sustains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="f2b0d75b-5269-4ff2-968e-6b31adab60dd">
      <data key="d3">The policy requires premium payments until age 100, ensuring continuous coverage throughout the insured’s lifetime. This long-term commitment enables the designated beneficiary, David Chen, to receive the full death benefit upon Margaret’s passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Since premiums continue until age 100, the policyholder may choose to convert the policy into Paid-Up Insurance at any point before maturity, eliminating future premium obligations while retaining a reduced death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
