    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="aa7737fa-2c32-4ee2-8244-f4f6917dedc8">
      <data key="d3">The provision allowing the Chen Family Trust to receive the full death benefit upon the primary beneficiary’s predecease reflects a structural feature enabled by the existence of the underlying policy, such as the one issued by Guardian Family Protection Corp.</data>
      <data key="d4">implied by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a contingent beneficiary clause requiring the trust to receive the full death benefit upon the primary beneficiary's predecease reflects typical features found in participating whole life insurance policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="6798b2ae-9c41-40d4-a9ed-fcff5337565b">
      <data key="d3">If the primary beneficiary predeceases Margaret Rose Chen, the Chen Family Trust becomes entitled to receive the full death benefit, making the existence of Margaret Rose Chen as the insured essential to activating this provision.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="2798b517-d05d-4a9e-a451-d86e9388a002">
      <data key="d3">If the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured, the Chen Family Trust inherits the full $250,000 death benefit, confirming the significance of the stated face amount in determining payout outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="696e047c-d749-4525-a7f2-29da3bb3dbc5">
      <data key="d3">If David Chen predeceases Margaret Rose Chen, the Chen Family Trust inherits the entire death benefit, making his designation as primary beneficiary essential to triggering this outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="bf1f70a7-46ad-4ace-b4cd-c595e8d81ca6">
      <data key="d3">If David Chen dies before Margaret Rose Chen, the Chen Family Trust becomes entitled to the full death benefit due to its designation as the contingent beneficiary; this outcome relies on David having been legally recognized as the primary beneficiary through marriage.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="e30d5ff9-c327-44ac-844c-18f5f947e1ea">
      <data key="d3">If the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured, the contingency clause activates, allowing the Chen Family Trust to receive the full death benefit based on its designation as the contingent beneficiary.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers benefit transfer</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951" target="f2b0d75b-5269-4ff2-968e-6b31adab60dd">
      <data key="d3">When the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured, the death benefit transfers entirely to the contingent beneficiary, meaning David Chen does not receive any portion unless he outlives the insured.</data>
      <data key="d4">predecessor condition</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="368a574e-130c-4534-ae7e-56ccf15ec292" target="cc4ee768-e80c-4370-82a3-99c192f12951">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">governs payout condition</data>
    </edge>
