    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="6a9057b6-de53-41f4-bd52-a33c3e2af728">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="01755d5d-95ca-4e38-8a46-6f1075c7c487">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="05eda54c-8287-4646-84a2-a24c8bd8d036">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="7a2400aa-0b7a-485f-9fdf-2b105dafc5d6">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="aa7737fa-2c32-4ee2-8244-f4f6917dedc8">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Cash Surrender Value clarifies a critical component of the policy’s benefits, which is part of the overall framework established by the policy’s issuance detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">defined by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">Knowing that cash surrender value exists supports the classification of the policy as participating whole life, as such value is a hallmark of participating policies.</data>
      <data key="d4">implied by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3">
      <data key="d3">Cash surrender value represents the monetary benefit received when terminating the policy; it accumulates based on factors including premium payments like the $3,240 annual contribution, though its definition stands independently from specific premium amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Cash Surrender Value in fact_sentence_1 is clarified by fact_sentence_2, which specifies that it equals the cash value after deducting outstanding loans and surrender fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">The availability of Cash Surrender Value allows the policyholder to use that value toward purchasing Paid-Up Insurance, effectively transitioning from a fully paying policy to one with no future premium obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value represents the accumulated equity in the policy, which serves as the foundation for securing a policy loan. Without a positive cash surrender value, a loan cannot be granted.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="29b4269d-f2dc-4371-857c-c53041540b11">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value is a benefit tied to the specific policy identified by the policy number, providing financial value if the policyholder surrenders the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">refers to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value enables borrowers to access funds through policy loans once sufficient value has accumulated, supporting the ability described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">The first fact establishes the meaning of cash surrender value, while the second specifies its actual guaranteed amount at Year 10, illustrating a concrete example of the concept within the policy’s timeline.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value informs the maximum loanable amount under the policy, which in turn affects the reduction of the death benefit due to outstanding loans and interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value enables borrowers to access funds via policy loans, while the 5% annual interest rate governs the cost of such borrowing, making the two interdependent aspects of the same financial feature.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">The definition of cash surrender value provides the foundational metric used to determine the maximum allowable loan amount under the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">The definition of cash surrender value in fact_sentence_1 explains what the figure mentioned in fact_sentence_2 represents—the actual payout if the policy were surrendered at Year 20.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value enables borrowers to access funds via policy loans, but compounded interest increases repayment obligations, reducing future cash availability and potentially diminishing the net payout upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value serves as the base amount available upon policy termination, but it is reduced by any outstanding loans and accumulated interest, which directly affect the actual payout received.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="38982992-4c11-4f86-a368-5f7251a9da9d" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines and pays cash surrender value</data>
    </edge>
