    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">Understanding how Cash Surrender Value is calculated depends on knowing the policy has accumulated cash value—a core attribute of participating whole life insurance, which supports the validity of such calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on accumulated cash value derived from premiums like the $3,240 annual payment, but it does not directly depend on the premium itself beyond its role in funding growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="52774065-26b0-46d4-8e62-adc712669781">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value formula includes adjustments for loans and charges, which may affect how much is received upon policy maturity on July 8, 2078.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 depends on the conceptual understanding of Cash Surrender Value introduced in fact_sentence_1 to provide its precise computation method.</data>
      <data key="d4">calculates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on accumulated cash value, which may be influenced by dividends received. However, dividends themselves do not directly determine surrender value calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value relates to potential financial proceeds if the policy is terminated; it informs decisions about conversion to paid-up insurance by determining available funds after deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">The presence of a policy loan reduces the cash value used in calculating the cash surrender value, making the loan a factor that diminishes the final surrender amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value from the policy supports the extended term insurance benefit by providing the funding mechanism when premiums cease. Without sufficient cash value, extended term insurance would not be viable.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="4efbedc6-1cfd-4358-ac83-80bd56506e46">
      <data key="d3">The concept of deducting outstanding loans appears in both the cash surrender value and death benefit calculations, showing that loan balances affect financial outcomes regardless of whether the policy ends via surrender or death.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">The cash surrender value, defined as cash value minus loans and surrender charges, determines the funds available to extend term insurance coverage without additional premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Cash Surrender Value informs financial decisions during policy lapse, including whether to opt for Extended Term Insurance instead. It provides a baseline for evaluating alternatives like extended coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Cash Surrender Value clarifies what the policyholder would receive when choosing the non-forfeiture option of cash surrender, making it essential for interpreting the implications of fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="5ea73efa-2572-4665-a567-0bc08cfeff08">
      <data key="d3">The concept of subtracting outstanding loans from a monetary value in fact_sentence_1 aligns with the deduction applied when paying out the death benefit in fact_sentence_2, showing consistency in handling loan offsets across policy terminations.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Cash Surrender Value informs the financial outcome tied to terminating the policy early, while Extended Term Insurance offers a non-monetary alternative that maintains protection without additional premiums, making it a complementary choice during lapse events.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary choice</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Cash Surrender Value informs the financial outcome tied to terminating the policy, while Reduced Paid-Up Insurance offers an alternative path maintaining some coverage without ongoing premiums. They represent distinct yet related non-forfeiture options.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Cash Surrender Value informs the basis for selecting Non-Forfeiture Options like Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, where the policy’s cash value determines the new benefit level upon stopping premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">The concept of Cash Surrender Value, defined by subtracting loans and fees from the cash value, determines the exact amount available when terminating the policy via cash surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value depends on unpaid loans and fees, similar to how reinstatement requires paying back overdue premiums with interest, linking both scenarios through financial liabilities tied to policy status changes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff">
      <data key="d3">The definition of Cash Surrender Value depends on subtracting outstanding loans, which aligns with the requirement in reinstatement to repay such loans with interest, showing continuity in loan handling across different policy events.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="b3ac5002-b47d-45fd-8c6f-813289686f71">
      <data key="d3">The concept of cash surrender value relates to terminating a policy and receiving funds, whereas reinstatement involves restoring a lapsed policy. These processes represent opposite ends of policy management—one exits, the other revives.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041" target="0f2cfa5e-fb62-4758-8fe0-1102a3d97086">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a cash surrender value implies that withdrawing from the policy later incurs specific financial calculations, whereas the 30-day free look provides an earlier opportunity to cancel entirely and get a full refund before such obligations arise.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
