    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are possible only because the policy is participating whole life, meaning the policyholder shares in the company’s surplus earnings through periodic distributions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3">
      <data key="d3">Dividends represent possible returns based on policyholder contributions, including the $3,240 annual premium, but do not rely on its exact figure for validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">derives from</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute to the growth of the policy’s cash value, which in turn affects the cash surrender value after deductions for loans and fees.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases cash value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are returns of premiums declared annually, but their actual determination depends on the insurer's financial experience, such as mortality, expenses, and investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">Dividends from the policy may increase the cash value over time via paid-up additions, contributing to the overall growth reflected in the guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Dividends increase the policy’s cash surrender value, thereby expanding the pool from which loans can be drawn under the 90% cap specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">Dividends may increase the policy’s cash value over time, contributing to the achievement of the guaranteed cash value at Year 10.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">Dividends increase the policy’s cash value over time, enhancing the basis for future policy loans. This supports the ability described in fact_sentence_2 to borrow against accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute to increasing the policy’s cash value and paid-up additions, which in turn affect the maximum loanable amount under the policy. This makes dividend performance indirectly relevant to the effective use and cost of policy loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly relevant</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute to increasing the policy’s cash surrender value, which helps mitigate reductions caused by outstanding loans and accrued interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute to increasing the policy’s cash value and paid-up additions, which indirectly affects the total death benefit available before deductions for loans and interest. Thus, while not directly altering loan impacts, dividends enhance the base upon which loan reductions operate.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute to increasing the policy’s cash value and paid-up additions, which in turn affect the maximum loanable amount and influence the accumulation of compounded interest on borrowed funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
