      <data key="d3">Dividends being based on the company’s experience depend on the existence of a participating policy issued by the company, such as the one described here.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">The company’s experience determines dividend payouts, which only occur because the policy is classified as participating.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">Dividends increase the policy’s cash value over time, which indirectly supports the availability of higher policy loan amounts. This creates a background condition enabling more substantial borrowing capacity.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The company's experience directly influences whether and how much in dividends are distributed; without favorable experience, no dividends would be declared despite eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Dividends earned from favorable company experience can increase the policy’s cash value, potentially enabling the policyholder to convert to paid-up insurance without future premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
