    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="aa7737fa-2c32-4ee2-8244-f4f6917dedc8">
      <data key="d3">The presence of policy loans indicates that the insurer offers flexible borrowing mechanisms tied to the policy’s cash value, confirming it as a participating whole life product.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="29b4269d-f2dc-4371-857c-c53041540b11">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a policy loan facility, backed by cash value, applies specifically to policies like the one identified by the given policy number.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="82aeed9b-92d1-465a-b1fa-fc66540d9d53">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a policy loan option depends on the policy having accumulated cash value, which is characteristic of participating whole life insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="e1c25cef-f1a5-45b6-bce9-aecb6d7ba9a3">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans depend on the presence of sufficient cash value, which accumulates from consistent premium payments like the $3,240 annual payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="93e5c855-70f6-47b8-99fd-a2bc45122e25">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans rely on available cash value built up from consistent premium payments; therefore, the ability to take such loans assumes periodic premium payments, including annual ones.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="874ec04d-ba44-4087-bca5-6ad2e68a63c7">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans are enabled by the presence of accumulated cash surrender value, which builds up gradually through consistent premium payments over time. Since premiums are required until age 100, this prolonged payment schedule supports the growth of cash value necessary to secure such loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">facilitated by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans utilize the cash surrender value as collateral; therefore, the ability to take such a loan depends directly on having a sufficient cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans utilize the cash value as collateral, thereby reducing the net cash value available for surrender, which directly influences how much is ultimately payable upon surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="7f9e8133-9ea9-4e40-b2c8-cccc14df47a1">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans draw from the cash value built up through premiums and dividends, meaning the ability to take such loans depends on prior accumulation driven partly by dividend income.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">A Policy Loan utilizes the cash value as collateral, enabling funds withdrawal. In contrast, Paid-Up Insurance converts cash value into guaranteed coverage without future payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 supports the ability to secure a policy loan, as lenders typically allow borrowers to access funds based on this value. Thus, fact_sentence_2 strengthens the practical applicability of fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a guaranteed cash value of $28,450 at Year 10 supports the ability to secure a policy loan, enabling borrowers to access funds against that accumulated value without terminating coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how policy loans work using cash value, while fact_sentence_2 clarifies the specific cap—90% of cash surrender value—that defines the extent of those loans, making it a key constraint on the process described earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans utilize accumulated cash value as collateral, and if not repaid, reduce the death benefit through outstanding principal and accrued interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The use of cash value as collateral for a policy loan (fact_sentence_1) is reinforced by the detail that loan interest compounds annually (fact_sentence_2), affecting repayment dynamics and reducing future benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a policy loan relying on cash value as collateral is directly relevant to the deduction of outstanding loans and accrued interest from the cash surrender value, ensuring alignment with policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a policy loan facility, as stated in fact_sentence_1, is enabled only after one year of policy duration, as specified in fact_sentence_2, making the two facts temporally and functionally linked.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
