      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="98bc2512-31bc-4f3c-8650-bdb3911cb35d">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s guaranteed cash value increase over time is enhanced by its tax-deferred status, allowing earnings to accumulate without immediate taxation.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the existence of a guaranteed cash value accumulation schedule. Fact_sentence_2 specifies a particular outcome under that schedule, confirming its predictability and validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that the policy’s cash value increases based on a guaranteed schedule. The second sentence specifies a key milestone under that schedule—the guaranteed value of $71,200 at Year 20—which illustrates how the accumulation progresses over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth schedule provides a baseline projection for cash value accumulation, but actual results may surpass this if dividends are credited. Dividend allocations increase the total cash value above what’s guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value buildup provides the foundation upon which paid-up additions increase the policy's value. This allocation method enhances long-term growth based on the scheduled accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed buildup of cash value enables future borrowing privileges. Without the accumulation described in sentence 1, the ability to borrow in sentence 2 would not exist.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value provides the foundation for determining the maximum loanable amount, which is set at 90% of the current cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed buildup of cash value provides the basis for allowing policyholders to take out loans, which in turn impacts the final payout by reducing either the death benefit or cash surrender value when not repaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value provides the basis for eligible policy loans, enabling borrowers to access funds tied to the policy’s increasing value. Interest accumulation on those loans further impacts the net value available upon withdrawal or death.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed buildup of cash value provides the foundation for paid-up additions, which increase the total death benefit. This accumulated value directly influences the final payout when the insured passes away.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value enables the existence of a cash surrender value, which serves as collateral for loans. Outstanding loans and accrued interest are subtracted from this value, making it essential that the cash value has been built through the guaranteed schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed buildup of cash value relies partly on the use of dividends through paid-up additions, which enhance long-term growth potential beyond fixed projections.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value provides the basis for determining how much a policyholder may borrow. When debt surpasses this accumulated value, it triggers policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fab7ed7e-8a81-472a-87d6-d2f3b56c0e50" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">reaches known value at end of year 20</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="555b991a-107d-4fdf-baaf-3d711d94e4a4" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has guaranteed cash value growth</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0d2d5965-7525-4ac8-8554-6d0f74f3be3e" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is the guaranteed growth rate</data>
    </edge>
