    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $28,450 at Year 10 serves as empirical support for the assertion that the policy’s cash value increases according to a fixed, predictable schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $28,450 at Year 10 demonstrates the outcome of sustained tax-deferred growth over time within the policy’s structure.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value grows from $28,450 at Year 10 to $71,200 by Year 20, reflecting sustained accumulation on a fixed schedule.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $28,450 by Year 10 serves as a minimum benchmark, but actual accumulated value may rise above this level when credited dividends are applied.</data>
      <data key="d4">exceeds</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value reaching $28,450 by Year 10 reflects the policy’s long-term growth potential, which becomes accessible only after sufficient duration. This accumulation supports eligibility for borrowing once the policy has been active for one year.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value projection at Year 10 reflects accumulated gains from premium payments and reinvested dividends, including those applied via paid-up additions. This illustrates how the dividend allocation method supports long-term value growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $28,450 at Year 10 establishes a measurable basis for determining how much a policyholder may borrow under the policy’s terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 10 represents an accumulation milestone that influences the maximum potential loanable amount, thereby affecting future obligations like those described in fact_sentence_2 regarding loan deductions from the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 10 represents an accumulated sum before considering liabilities like loans. Outstanding loans and accrued interest reduce the net cash surrender value that would otherwise be accessible.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $28,450 by Year 10 establishes a baseline for the policy’s financial strength, against which potential loan balances may be compared. If borrowers exceed this value through accumulating debts, the policy risks termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional threshold</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 10 ($28,450) exemplifies what is meant by cash surrender value, directly grounding the abstract definition in measurable policy performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">example of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 10 reflects accumulated benefits, potentially enhanced by periodic dividends declared under the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans based on cash value ensures liquidity during the policy term, allowing holders like Margaret Rose Chen to utilize the $28,450 guaranteed cash value at Year 10 through borrowed amounts secured by it.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">A key condition enabling paid-up insurance is having adequate cash value buildup; the guaranteed $28,450 at Year 10 reflects progress toward meeting this threshold, making the transition feasible.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="86a532f6-3f69-4dcb-855f-28b484c2d7d3" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">has guaranteed value at</data>
