    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">The second sentence gives a precise figure ($71,200) representing the accumulated cash value at Year 20, which serves as empirical validation of the guaranteed growth process described in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value reaching $71,200 at Year 20 reflects the outcome of sustained tax-deferred growth throughout the policy’s term.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">The increase from $28,450 at Year 10 to $71,200 at Year 20 demonstrates long-term growth based on the policy’s guaranteed accumulation plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">follows</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 by Year 20 acts as a minimum benchmark, but actual accumulated value may surpass it if dividends are credited.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 20 depends partly on how dividends are used; allocating them to paid-up additions increases future cash value. This choice enhances long-term accumulation potential.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 is partially driven by the reinvestment of dividends into paid-up additions, which increase the policy's overall value over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 sets the basis for determining the maximum allowable loan, enabling borrowers to access up to 90% of this amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value reaching $71,200 by Year 20 represents a milestone that makes borrowing possible under the policy terms. This accumulation supports the feasibility of loan provisions outlined later.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 20 reflects the total accumulation before considering external factors like loans. Loan interest that compounds annually reduces available cash value and death benefits when unpaid, thereby impacting the net outcome from the stated cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 by Year 20 establishes a critical threshold that determines if accumulated debt might cause policy termination. This figure enables assessment of risk related to borrowing beyond available equity.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 20 reflects accumulated growth under the policy terms, but if loans are taken and interest accrues, the actual net value could decrease due to compounding debt.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 establishes the maximum available basis for policyholder loans, which may subsequently affect the final payout. Outstanding loans and accrued interest are subtracted from the total death benefit, making the initial cash accumulation relevant to the ultimate settlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 may be reduced if borrowers have outstanding loans with accumulated interest, which are subtracted from the cash surrender value when claims are made.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value at Year 20 provides a benchmark for the policy’s growth, influencing the extent of available loans that may affect the final death benefit calculation. This contextual information helps frame the financial state underlying the death benefit determination.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 exemplifies the practical application of the cash surrender value concept described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The guaranteed cash value of $71,200 at Year 20 reflects the policy’s accumulated value, which complements the potential impact of future dividends on total policy worth.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that policy loans use cash value as collateral, so knowing the precise guaranteed cash value at Year 20 allows accurate assessment of available loan amounts, thereby grounding the concept in measurable financial parameters provided in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">A key feature enabling paid-up insurance is the accumulation of guaranteed cash value over time, which ensures that even without ongoing payments, the policy retains value and coverage through built-up reserves.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
