    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute extra value beyond the guaranteed schedule, meaning the actual cash value exceeds projections set by the fixed guarantee. Without dividends, the value would remain at the guaranteed level.</data>
      <data key="d4">exceeds</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">Dividend credits can boost the cash value beyond the guaranteed levels, enhancing the benefits of tax-deferred growth already established in the first statement.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">Dividend allocations can boost the cash value beyond the guaranteed $28,450 at Year 10, meaning the initial guarantee is not necessarily the final outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">Non-guaranteed dividends can increase the cash value beyond the guaranteed $71,200 at Year 20, making the stated guarantee a floor rather than a ceiling.</data>
      <data key="d4">exceeds</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">The presence of non-guaranteed dividends—possible only in a participating policy—explains why the actual cash value might surpass the guaranteed amounts outlined in the projection.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The potential for higher-than-guaranteed cash value relies on dividend credits, but since dividends are not guaranteed, this increase cannot be assured.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of actual cash value exceeding the guaranteed amount relies on dividend credits, which themselves depend on the insurer's financial results.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The potential increase in cash value beyond guaranteed levels stems from dividend allocations, such as those directed into paid-up additions, which enhance the policy’s growth over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f">
      <data key="d3">The potential for actual cash value to surpass guarantees stems from dividend allocations, such as those credited under the "Accumulate at Interest" option, which grow over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">The use of paid-up additions as the dividend option increases the policy’s cash value over time by adding additional coverage, contributing to the possibility of exceeding the guaranteed cash value amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Higher actual cash value due to dividend credits increases the cash surrender value, thereby raising the maximum loan amount allowed under the policy terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The actual cash value exceeding guarantees due to dividends influences the total available funds that could be used for borrowing, indirectly affecting loan calculations. However, it does not directly determine how loans impact the death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">Higher cash value due to dividend credits increases the margin before loan balance triggers policy termination, reducing the risk of cancellation.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The presence of dividend credits increases the cash value above guarantees, potentially affecting the total available for borrowing. However, if loans are taken, those increased funds could still be reduced by loan deductions and interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The actual cash value exceeding guarantees due to dividends affects the total available equity that influences the calculation of the final death benefit. However, this does not alter the formulaic deduction of loans and interest specified in the payout condition.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d3">The actual cash value exceeding the guaranteed amount relies on dividend credits, which themselves depend on the insurer’s performance, including mortality experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add" target="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328">
      <data key="d3">The actual cash value exceeding guarantees relies on dividends being credited, which are determined by the insurer’s financial results, including its expense experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
