    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Being a participating policy allows for the receipt of dividends, which contribute to increasing the cash value beyond its guaranteed growth path.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">The policy being participating implies it offers potential returns tied to the insurer’s financial success, which is reflected in annually declared dividends based on investment results.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328">
      <data key="d3">The policy being participating implies it may issue dividends, which are influenced by the insurer's financial results, including expense experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d3">The policy being participating implies it offers potential returns via dividends, which are influenced by the insurer’s financial performance, including mortality experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="579250ef-d01a-46bc-bff9-32a1bfc0f959">
      <data key="d3">The policy's status as participating allows for potential dividends, including the option to receive them as a cash payment. This choice reflects how dividends from a participating policy can be distributed.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is participating implies potential dividend distributions, but sentence 2 specifies that such dividends are not guaranteed, highlighting an important limitation on expected returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="c44535a0-156c-43cf-9dbe-de157fb94427">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy is participating, it generates dividends that can be used in various ways, including reducing future premiums through the Premium Reduction option.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Being a participating policy means the policyholder may receive dividends, which contribute to increasing the cash surrender value over time. This growth affects the basis for calculating the maximum loan amount, which is set at 90% of the current cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Since the policy is participating, it generates dividends that can be applied in various ways. Currently, these dividends are directed toward increasing the policy’s coverage through paid-up additions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The policy's status as participating enables the distribution of dividends, which can be applied toward purchasing additional coverage through paid-up additions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The fact that this is a participating policy implies potential for additional benefits like dividends used for paid-up additions, contributing to long-term value accumulation. This context supports why outstanding loans and accrued interest are subtracted from the death benefit, as such features influence the net payout calculation.</data>
      <data key="d4">contextual supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The policy's participating nature enables features such as dividend allocations and access to loans, which underpin the mechanism where interest accrues on unpaid loan balances.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f">
      <data key="d3">The policy being participating allows for the distribution of dividends, such as those accumulated at interest, which enhances long-term cash value growth through compounding returns on unclaimed dividends.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The policy's status as participating means it may generate dividends used for paid-up additions, contributing to overall cash value growth. This increased value affects the available cash surrender value, which is reduced by outstanding loans and accrued interest when claims are made.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The policy's status as participating enables dividend allocation toward paid-up additions, which contribute to the total death benefit. This supports the calculation described in fact_sentence_2 but is not required for its validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The fact that the policy is participating implies access to dividends that increase its cash value over time. This higher cash value provides collateral for loans, making it more likely that total indebtedness could eventually surpass the available cash value if loans grow unchecked.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables risk</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
