    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="ef71e332-02c1-4281-9b9a-31f2352051d2">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="3b22ad5c-e601-4cac-bb4e-0085263a8ef9">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">Dividends in a participating policy are typically tied to the insurer’s results—such as favorable mortality outcomes—which justifies why such policies distribute earnings to holders.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are influenced by the insurer’s mortality experience, which directly affects whether additional cash value accrues beyond guaranteed levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The potential for annual dividends depends on the insurer’s actual mortality results, but since such outcomes vary, dividends are not assured.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains that dividends depend on the insurer’s mortality performance, while fact sentence 2 adds that investment returns also influence dividend amounts. Together, they illustrate multiple contributing factors to dividend calculations.</data>
      <data key="d4">complemented by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="579250ef-d01a-46bc-bff9-32a1bfc0f959">
      <data key="d3">The first sentence states that dividends depend on the insurer’s mortality performance, establishing how dividends are generated. The second sentence outlines one possible use of such dividends—the recipient receiving them directly as cash payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="c44535a0-156c-43cf-9dbe-de157fb94427">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are generated based on the insurer’s mortality performance, creating the financial resource that can be used to reduce future premiums under certain options like Premium Reduction.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are generated based on the insurer’s mortality experience, providing the financial foundation for distribution options such as Paid-Up Additions.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are generated based on the insurer’s performance, particularly mortality results, creating the potential for funds to be used in various ways. One such method involves leaving dividends with the insurer to grow through accumulated interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are determined annually based on the insurer's performance, particularly mortality experience. These dividends are then used to purchase additional paid-up insurance coverage under the chosen dividend option.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">Dividends enhance the policy’s cash value over time, providing more equity that could be used as collateral for loans. This increased cash value affects the balance against which outstanding loans and interest are subtracted.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">Dividends, influenced by mortality experience, increase paid-up additions, which contribute to the total death benefit. This enhances the final payout described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4924eb8f-625f-4941-9ed5-ae04e53d7569" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
