    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="6ec393b8-db15-4734-a015-daba75fbfe37">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="2a864e47-89ae-480f-91d0-1f3ff29f6086">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are influenced by the insurer's investment success, and when distributed, they contribute to increasing the cash value above its guaranteed level.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">Annual dividends are possible because the policy is participating, allowing policyholders to receive distributions from the insurer’s surplus earnings.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 notes that investment gains affect dividend payouts, complementing fact sentence 1, which identifies mortality results as another key determinant of dividends.</data>
      <data key="d4">complemented by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="579250ef-d01a-46bc-bff9-32a1bfc0f959">
      <data key="d3">The potential for annual dividends depends on the insurer’s financial results, and one such payout mechanism is the Cash Payment option, allowing immediate receipt by the policyholder.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="c44535a0-156c-43cf-9dbe-de157fb94427">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are determined by the insurer’s financial results and can be used to lower upcoming premiums through the Premium Reduction option.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f">
      <data key="d3">The declaration of annual dividends depends on the insurer’s financial results, enabling options like accumulating them at interest instead of receiving immediate payment.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The potential for annual dividends, contingent on the insurer’s financial results, enables the availability of the Paid-Up Additions option, allowing policyholders to increase their coverage using unallocated dividends.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The potential for annual dividends depends on the insurer’s financial results, but since they are not guaranteed, actual payouts remain uncertain and discretionary.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are not guaranteed and depend on the insurer’s financial results, but when declared, they are currently directed into paid-up additions to increase the policy’s cash value and death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">Dividends enhance the policy’s cash value through paid-up additions, indirectly supporting the financial cushion against loan reductions. This helps preserve the death benefit when loans are present.</data>
      <data key="d4">indirectly supports</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Dividends contribute to increasing the cash surrender value over time, which directly affects the maximum loan amount available under the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="dd1a2726-c66b-40af-86ea-a9958f2a897a" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">based on investment experience</data>
    </edge>
