    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">Dividends from a participating policy are contingent upon the insurer's performance, particularly its expenses, reinforcing why such policies offer potential returns beyond guarantees.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are contingent upon favorable expense experience, enabling them to boost the cash value beyond guaranteed levels over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are contingent upon the insurer's financial performance, specifically expense experience. This creates the possibility for dividends to be used under options like accumulating at interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="579250ef-d01a-46bc-bff9-32a1bfc0f959">
      <data key="d3">The existence of annual dividends depends on the insurer’s financial performance, particularly its expenses. One possible use of such dividends is receiving them directly via a cash payment option.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="c44535a0-156c-43cf-9dbe-de157fb94427">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are generated based on the insurer's financial performance, specifically its expense experience. These dividends can then be used to reduce future premiums through the Premium Reduction option.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are influenced by the insurer’s expenses, creating the financial basis for distributing surplus funds. These dividends can then be applied toward purchasing additional insurance through the Paid-Up Additions option.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The potential for annual dividends depends on the insurer’s financial performance, but since such dividends are not guaranteed, they remain speculative rather than contractual obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Dividends are generated based on the insurer's financial performance, particularly expense experience, enabling them to be distributed. These dividends are currently directed into paid-up additions, increasing the policy’s future benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">Dividends influence the growth of paid-up additions, which in turn affect the total death benefit. However, the specific timing or impact of dividend declarations is not directly tied to the settlement process described in sentence 2.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
