      <data key="d3">Receiving dividends as a cash payment requires the insurer to declare them first, typically based on favorable expense experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="579250ef-d01a-46bc-bff9-32a1bfc0f959" target="c44535a0-156c-43cf-9dbe-de157fb94427">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes receiving dividends as immediate cash, while fact sentence 2 explains using dividends to lower upcoming premiums. Both are separate methods for utilizing dividends without affecting each other's validity.</data>
