    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Dividends allocated via "Accumulate at Interest" contribute directly to increasing cash value beyond guaranteed levels, thereby enabling the scenario described in the first sentence.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">The availability of an "Accumulate at Interest" dividend option demonstrates how the policy’s participation feature enables additional financial benefits beyond the base premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d3">The availability of dividends, influenced by factors like mortality experience, enables options such as accumulating them at interest, providing growth beyond the initial payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">Accumulating dividends at interest requires that dividends first be declared, making it contingent upon the insurer’s ability to issue such payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328">
      <data key="d3">The availability of dividend accumulation at interest requires that dividends have been declared, which occurs based on the insurer's expense experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The option to accumulate dividends at interest implies that dividends may occur, but since they are explicitly stated as non-guaranteed, this highlights the speculative nature of such allocations.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="20487c89-e0e7-4387-abc3-4e1f3259ca1f" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The dividend accumulation option increases paid-up additions, which are included in the final death benefit calculation described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
