      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions serve as a method that contributes to the overall accumulation of cash value over time, aligning with the guaranteed growth schedule outlined in the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions utilize dividends to expand coverage and cash value, enhancing the very growth process enabled by tax-deferred accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions increase the policy's overall value by adding more coverage using dividends, contributing to higher cash value totals such as the $28,450 projected at Year 10.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions, which use dividends to buy extra coverage, contribute incrementally to the buildup of cash value, ultimately supporting the achievement of the $71,200 guarantee at Year 20.</data>
      <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Dividend payments used for paid-up additions boost the policy's cash value, contributing to actual values exceeding the guaranteed projections.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions serve as a key mechanism by which dividends from a participating policy increase the policy’s overall value.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d3">The availability of Paid-Up Additions depends on the declaration of dividends, which are influenced by factors including the insurer’s mortality experience.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">The existence of the Paid-Up Additions option relies on the prior possibility of declaring annual dividends based on the insurer’s investment outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328">
      <data key="d3">The Paid-Up Additions option uses dividends to buy extra coverage, implying that such dividends must exist and be available—this depends on favorable expense performance by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The option to use dividends for paid-up additions implies that such benefits depend on receiving dividends, which themselves are not guaranteed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="c44535a0-156c-43cf-9dbe-de157fb94427">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 details how dividends fund new insurance through paid-up additions, contrasting with fact_sentence_1’s focus on lowering upcoming premiums. Each represents a separate strategy for utilizing dividends without direct causal linkage.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative use</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Paid-Up Additions increase the policy’s cash value and overall death benefit by adding more insurance coverage using dividends. This growth contributes to higher cash surrender value, which determines the upper limit for policy loans.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains what Paid-Up Additions means as a dividend option. Fact_sentence_2 confirms that this particular option is actively chosen and applied within the current policy configuration.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions increase the policy’s cash value over time, thereby raising the buffer against loan balances exceeding the cash surrender value, delaying potential policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions increase the policy’s overall value and contribute to the death benefit, but if loans exist, they reduce it. This creates an indirect link where the growth mechanism affects the net payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">Paid-up additions increase the total insured value by adding incremental coverage using dividends, which directly contributes to the death benefit calculated upon claim. Without such additions, the final payout would be lower than stated.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
