      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Dividend allocations directed toward paid-up additions enhance the policy's cash value, making it more likely that actual cash value exceeds the guaranteed projections.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">The decision to allocate dividends to paid-up additions relies on the policy being participating, as only such policies generate dividends eligible for reinvestment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="f7f0f5d5-2d0e-4014-aa5a-76bbb9faf578">
      <data key="d3">The selection of "Paid-Up Additions" as the dividend option means that any declared dividends are automatically reinvested into increasing the policy’s cash value through additional coverage. This choice depends on whether dividends are actually issued, which hinges on the insurer’s mortality results.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">The choice to allocate dividends to paid-up additions relies on the occurrence of annual dividends, which are determined by the insurer’s investment performance.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="23c1dfbe-c779-47ed-b0fc-14e97169d328">
      <data key="d3">The decision to allocate dividends to paid-up additions reflects an active use of available dividends, which themselves depend on favorable expense experience reported by the insurer.</data>
      <data key="d4">utilizes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The decision to use Paid-Up Additions as the dividend option implies reliance on receiving dividends, which are explicitly stated as non-guaranteed, making the effectiveness of this strategy inherently uncertain.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Paid-Up Additions as the active dividend option implies that the policyholder has opted into the mechanism described in fact_sentence_1, where dividends fund additional insurance coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The use of Paid-Up Additions increases the policy’s cash value over time, thereby enhancing the borrower’s ability to access funds through loans once the policy has been active for one year.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">The use of Paid-Up Additions boosts the policy’s cash surrender value over time, increasing the pool available for borrowing. This makes the maximum allowable loan amount more substantial as the cash value grows due to dividend allocations.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">Paid-Up Additions increase the policy’s cash value over time, making it more likely that loan balances could exceed this value, potentially leading to policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">Paid-Up Additions enhance the policy’s death benefit by increasing its overall value through dividend allocations. However, if loans remain unpaid, those gains may be offset because outstanding loan balances and interest directly reduce the final death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The selection of Paid-Up Additions as the dividend option results in additional coverage being added to the policy without requiring extra premiums, thereby increasing the total death benefit available when claims are made.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="17ba33d2-5ff6-4e08-89eb-da473681d535" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is increased by</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4851fb21-5f3a-4a1c-b4b3-8983a5ab8851" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bbc52f62-dcd5-4854-b91c-5c57d6d941be" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">marks a point where cumulative effect of</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0fe07920-4002-41c3-a4b1-94392de059bd" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">marks a point where cumulative effect of</data>
    </edge>
