      <data key="d4">period</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="45fafa3a-a193-4a80-afa7-edf0161ab2f8">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="2d87c031-6f50-4539-abde-69127852e03a">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">The right to borrow after one year depends on having sufficient cash value built up, which is ensured by the guaranteed schedule mentioned in sentence 1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">Policyholders' ability to borrow against the cash value after one year relies on the prior accumulation of value, which is facilitated by its tax-deferred growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">After one year of coverage, policyholders gain the right to borrow against the accumulating cash value, including amounts like the $28,450 expected at Year 10, though such access requires meeting minimum tenure requirements.</data>
      <data key="d4">postdates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">The eligibility to borrow after one year allows policyholders to access funds built through the gradual increase in cash value, including the eventual $71,200 at Year 20.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">The availability of borrowing after one year depends on accumulated cash value, which is increased by allocating dividends to Paid-Up Additions—making this choice essential for building loan eligibility.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">After one year, a policyholder gains access to borrowing privileges based on accumulated cash value, and any such loan incurs an annual compound interest rate of 5%.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional rate</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">After one year, borrowers gain access to funds based on their accumulated cash value, but the amount they can withdraw is limited to 90% of the current cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">After one year, a policyholder gains the right to borrow against the accumulated cash value. Any interest charged on such a loan is compounded by adding it back to the outstanding balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The right to borrow from the cash value after one year introduces financial flexibility but carries the risk that exceeding the cash value through accumulated debt triggers policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes risk of termination</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">After one year, a policyholder gains access to borrow against the cash value. Any borrowed amounts, along with compounded interest, reduce the available cash surrender value when the policy ends or is surrendered.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">After one year, borrowers gain access to the cash value, enabling them to take out loans that accrue interest over time through annual compounding.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d">
      <data key="d3">After a policyholder becomes eligible to borrow after one year, they have the option to pay interest on the loan annually, helping manage debt growth.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The right to borrow against the cash value after one year enables policyholders to withdraw funds, potentially increasing the debt owed on the policy. This affects the final death benefit by reducing it if loans remain unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">After one year, a policyholder gains access to borrow funds using accumulated cash value. Any borrowed amounts, along with accrued interest, are subtracted from the death benefit upon claim.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">Policy loans rely on the presence of a cash surrender value, meaning the availability of such value—as defined in fact_sentence_1—is essential for the functionality described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The option to borrow against cash value depends on its accumulation, which is influenced by dividends used for paid-up additions, thereby reinforcing the significance of dividend eligibility mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Access to cash value via policy loans after one year facilitates the transition to paid-up insurance by providing funds that support continued coverage without additional premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the timeline requirement for accessing policy loans, which directly supports the applicability of the loan mechanism described in fact_sentence_1 once the policy has been active for one year.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4af95325-ef2e-40aa-a22a-710466715292" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">borrowed against</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="65daaac1-dcc1-4671-8a90-1ac18663338e" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a15724d0-a572-4cbd-a494-d373007b98b2" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is enabled by</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="45fafa3a-a193-4a80-afa7-edf0161ab2f8" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">increases when</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="2d87c031-6f50-4539-abde-69127852e03a" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">decreased by</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="0814f6b1-7220-49e3-abcf-0d78d9ce5720">
