    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">The availability of a loan up to 90% of the cash surrender value implies that the cash value has been accumulating over time through the guaranteed schedule described earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">The availability of loans up to 90% of the cash surrender value relies on the presence of an established cash value, which itself results from tax-deferred growth over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">The rule allowing loans up to 90% of the cash surrender value relies on actual accumulated values like the $28,450 guarantee at Year 10 to determine eligibility and limits.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">The policy's provision allowing loans up to 90% of the cash surrender value means that the accumulated cash value—such as the $71,200 at Year 20—is directly relevant to calculating borrowing capacity.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount being based on current cash surrender value means that any increase in cash value—such as through dividend credits—directly affects how much can be borrowed.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount being limited to 90% of the cash surrender value relies on the accumulation of cash value, which is enhanced by dividends from the participating nature of the policy. Thus, the policy's participatory status indirectly supports higher available loan amounts through increased cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit being tied to the cash surrender value means it indirectly reflects the long-term accumulation from factors like non-guaranteed dividends.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit depends on the current cash surrender value, which can be increased by annual dividends allocated to paid-up additions.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">The ability to borrow up to 90% of the cash surrender value depends on the accumulated value built through mechanisms like Paid-Up Additions. Thus, the loan cap is indirectly influenced by how dividends are reinvested into additional coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">The cap on loan amounts at 90% of cash surrender value depends on how much that value has grown through mechanisms like Paid-Up Additions, meaning the dividend choice directly influences the financial ceiling for borrowing.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The ability to borrow from the policy’s cash value is contingent upon having held the policy for at least one year, ensuring sufficient accumulation before accessing funds.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">A loan capped at 90% of the cash surrender value may lead to policy termination if the accumulated debt surpasses the available cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional consequence</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the cash surrender value, and when borrowed, it accrues interest at a fixed rate of 5% annually.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan allowed is capped at 90% of the cash surrender value, enabling borrowers to access significant funds during the policyholder’s lifetime. This borrowed amount directly affects the final payout upon death, as it reduces the total death benefit through repayment obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">A loan taken up to 90% of the cash surrender value reduces the policyholder’s available cash value over time due to accumulated interest and unpaid principal.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan allowed is based on the cash surrender value, enabling borrowers to access funds that support future interest accruals if not repaid promptly.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount being limited to 90% of the cash surrender value allows borrowers to access funds, but any such loan reduces future payouts. As stated, unpaid loans diminish the death benefit when claims are settled.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the cash surrender value, and since interest on these loans compounds annually, borrowers face increasing debt that impacts future policy benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">The rule limiting loans to 90% of the cash surrender value relies explicitly on the existence and meaning of that value as described in the first fact.</data>
