    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The 5% annual compound interest rate applies only when a policyholder borrows from the cash value, which becomes available after one year of policy ownership.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to loan</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">A 5% annual compound interest applies to loans taken against the policy’s cash surrender value, which limits how much can be borrowed relative to that value.</data>
      <data key="d4">applies to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The 5% annual interest rate applies consistently only because it compounds each year, meaning interest accrues on previously accumulated interest. This compounding behavior amplifies the total cost of borrowing over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d">
      <data key="d3">The 5% annual compound interest rate enables accumulated debt over time, and paying interest annually helps manage this growth while maintaining policy value integrity.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">The 5% annual compound interest rate on loans leads to accumulating debt that reduces the available cash surrender value when not repaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">A 5% annual compound interest rate on policy loans causes accumulated debt to grow rapidly, increasing the risk that total indebtedness may eventually exceed the cash surrender value, triggering policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The 5% annual interest rate allows accumulated interest from policy loans to increase the total loan balance over time through compounding.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The 5% annual compound interest rate on policy loans determines the amount of interest that accrues over time, which is deducted from the death benefit when claims are processed.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables calculation</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">A 5% annual compound interest rate applies to policyholder loans, leading to accumulating debt that reduces the available death benefit when not repaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">The 5% loan interest rate applies specifically to withdrawals from the cash surrender value, meaning the availability and use of this value depend on the stated interest conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">The 5% loan interest rate impacts the net benefit derived from policy loans, potentially reducing available cash value over time; however, it does not alter the conditions under which dividends are declared or distributed.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences cost</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">A 5% annual loan interest rate impacts the viability of choosing paid-up insurance by increasing the cost of borrowed funds, potentially reducing the net benefit compared to continuing premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
