    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="a0780392-3d45-41ef-8fd6-d62977ebe852">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">concept</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding of loan interest influences the effective depletion of the policy’s cash value over time, meaning that even though the guaranteed cash value reaches $71,200 by Year 20, actual accessible funds may decrease due to compounded debt obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The requirement for annual compounding of loan interest implies that such loans are available only when borrowing rights have vested, typically after one year of policy ownership.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding ensures that the stated 5% interest rate results in increasing debt beyond simple interest, making the effective growth of loan balance dependent on this periodic compounding process.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding of loan interest increases the effective cost of borrowing, meaning the actual available loan amount may be reduced by anticipated repayment burdens tied to the 90% cap.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The annual compounding of loan interest means that accumulated interest increases the total loan balance each year, leading to higher debt over time if not repaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d">
      <data key="d3">The annual compounding of loan interest creates a framework in which paying interest yearly becomes feasible and relevant. This periodicity allows borrowers to manage debt by making annual payments without immediate full repayment.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding of loan interest accelerates debt accumulation, increasing the likelihood that total indebtedness surpasses the cash value, triggering policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding increases the total loan balance over time, leading to larger deductions from the cash surrender value when the loan remains unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The annual compounding of loan interest increases the total debt owed by the policyholder, which directly reduces the final death benefit when claims are processed.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="676d3ef5-d991-4b39-a33e-ea3ec7cfb545">
      <data key="d3">The annual compounding of loan interest increases the outstanding debt, raising the risk that the policyholder cannot meet required payments within the 31-day grace period, potentially leading to policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">increases risk of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding increases the total loan balance over time, leading to larger deductions from the death benefit when claims are settled.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">Compounded loan interest erodes the effective cash surrender value by increasing liabilities tied to borrowed amounts, thereby decreasing the actual sum available should the policyholder choose to surrender the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces value of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">Compounded loan interest reduces the net death benefit and cash surrender value, potentially diminishing the overall impact of future dividends when calculating actual returns.</data>
      <data key="d4">impacts returns</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">Annual compounding of loan interest (fact_sentence_2) impacts the effective cost of borrowing against the policy’s cash value, which is central to the functionality of policy loans outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Compounded loan interest directly impacts whether a policyholder can achieve or sustain paid-up insurance, as rising debts diminish the net cash value used to fund such a state.</data>
      <data key="d4">affects status of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
