    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The availability of annual interest payments depends on first being allowed to take out a loan, which requires the policy to have been in force for one year.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">Annual payment of loan interest ensures compliance with the 5% compound interest requirement, preventing rapid erosion of cash value through unmanaged accumulation.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The possibility of paying interest annually depends on it being compounded annually, ensuring alignment between payment frequency and compounding intervals within the policy’s terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">Accrued interest from an unpaid loan reduces the cash surrender value over time, meaning that even if interest payments are made annually, failure to pay results in deductions from the policy’s cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">If interest on a policy loan is not paid annually, it may be added to the loan balance, increasing the total debt owed over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on a policy loan contributes to the reduction of the death benefit by increasing the total debt owed against the policy, which is deducted from the face amount and paid-up additions during settlement.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The ability to pay interest annually on a policy loan helps prevent accumulation of unpaid interest, reducing the risk of exceeding the cash value. This supports ongoing policy viability by mitigating conditions leading to termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">If interest on a policy loan is not paid annually, it compounds, increasing the total loan balance. This larger balance leads to greater reductions in the death benefit when deducted upon payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
