    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination occurs when indebtedness surpasses the available cash value, highlighting the importance of the cash value's growth—driven by tax-deferred compounding—as a safeguard against such outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">Excessive borrowing beyond the cash value causes policy termination, meaning the guaranteed accumulation of cash value serves as a threshold limiting allowable debt levels.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination occurs when indebtedness surpasses the available cash value, meaning that milestones like the $28,450 guarantee at Year 10 serve as critical thresholds beyond which the policy becomes vulnerable to lapse.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination due to exceeding cash value depends on knowing the actual cash value, such as the $71,200 guaranteed at Year 20, which defines the maximum allowable debt before default occurs.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination when indebtedness exceeds cash value implies that maintaining sufficient cash value—enhanced by dividends—is critical to avoiding loss of coverage.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">When a policy’s total indebtedness exceeds its cash value, termination occurs. Since this policy is participating and builds cash value through dividends, such a scenario depends on how aggressively borrowed funds accumulate relative to those gains.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional limit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="13b1ef68-ef2d-411e-9021-06ccea514adb">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination occurs if indebtedness surpasses cash value—a scenario made more probable when non-guaranteed dividends fail to materialize, thereby constraining cash value buildup needed to absorb loan balances.</data>
      <data key="d4">undermines safety net</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination upon exceeding cash value creates a risk that reduces the long-term effectiveness of paid-up additions, especially if borrowing increases significantly.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination due to exceeding cash value occurs when borrowing reduces the cash value below zero, an outcome influenced by prior growth from options like Paid-Up Additions.</data>
      <data key="d4">can lead to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">Exceeding the cash value with borrowed amounts results in policy termination, highlighting why access to borrowing is contingent on responsible use and timing post-issue.</data>
      <data key="d4">consequence of borrowing</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination occurs when debts exceed the cash value, meaning borrowers cannot access more than 90% of the cash surrender value without risking cancellation.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes termination</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination occurs when loan balances, including compounded interest at 5%, surpass the available cash value, meaning the interest rate is a key driver behind this outcome.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">Policy termination occurs if indebtedness exceeds cash value, a scenario made more probable by the annual compounding of loan interest on borrowed amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder fails to manage loan interest payments, accumulated debt may exceed the cash value, triggering automatic termination—a scenario where timely interest payments could have prevented failure.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">A policy terminates if the total owed—including principal and compounded interest—exceeds the available cash value. Interest being added to the loan balance is what drives this risk.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder's loans surpass the cash value, the policy ends. This termination directly affects the death benefit, which is reduced by any outstanding loans and accrued interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">When loans and interest accumulate, they decrease the cash surrender value, increasing the risk of exceeding the policy’s cash value. This sets the stage for termination if debts grow too large.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="676d3ef5-d991-4b39-a33e-ea3ec7cfb545">
      <data key="d3">When loan balance exceeds cash value, the policy risks termination. To prevent this, the holder must repay the shortfall within 31 days of receiving notification.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes termination</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">If the policyholder's debts exceed the available cash value, the policy ends prematurely, preventing any future payout. Otherwise, when a claim occurs, the insurer pays the adjusted death benefit by subtracting existing loans and interest from the base benefits.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="db64a37d-238c-4eda-82b8-816c25cd824e" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">threshold for policy termination</data>
    </edge>
