    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="9986f495-b32e-416c-9bee-9bd3fcfd38f1">
      <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit due to unpaid loans implies that such liabilities stem from access to previously accumulated cash value, reinforcing the importance of the guaranteed cash value growth described earlier.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="f0d953de-57de-4009-9c3c-a624848400bc">
      <data key="d3">Unpaid loans and accrued interest diminish the death benefit, reflecting the consequence of leveraging the previously tax-deferred-growing cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="4db504ec-839d-45cc-a54e-508072f29052">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans and accrued interest reduce the death benefit, meaning that if significant borrowing occurs before Year 10, it could diminish the effective value derived from the guaranteed $28,450 cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="8a5bb177-c6ec-43a8-ab9b-8642558f8120">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans and accrued interest reduce the death benefit, meaning that higher cash value—such as the guaranteed $71,200 at Year 20—can support larger loan amounts, thereby increasing the risk of reducing the final payout if left unpaid.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reducing the death benefit create a mechanism by which accumulated cash value—including any excess from dividends—is diminished, thus impacting the net payout even if the initial growth was stronger than expected.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="760d34d4-eb2d-414c-baa9-b87b4f1a8e93">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans and accrued interest reducing the death benefit reflect an important feature of the policy's financial structure. This mechanism is consistent with policies that accumulate cash value over time, including those that are participating, where built-up equity becomes available for borrowing.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="ea3ff14c-b0b2-41ce-b2c5-75781d17406d">
      <data key="d3">Loan balances and accrued interest directly diminish the death benefit, reducing the overall payout regardless of dividend contributions.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces value of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="39a1ab26-48c9-45c8-bbe9-0682552a3e65">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the death benefit, so any prior use of dividends to expand coverage via paid-up additions may help mitigate such reductions by increasing the base benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="e3e246c1-096d-44df-8e6e-335cc7374485">
      <data key="d3">Unpaid loans and accrued interest diminish the death benefit, counteracting the growth contributed by Paid-Up Additions, which were intended to boost the payout over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="982dcffc-8963-4a09-a00a-3a7afc345757">
      <data key="d3">Unpaid loans and accumulated interest directly impact the payout by reducing the death benefit, meaning that higher loan usage—up to 90% of the cash surrender value—leads to lower net proceeds for beneficiaries.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduced by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="3aa4a1e9-a805-4aee-a558-83457fd0e547">
      <data key="d3">Unpaid loans and their associated 5% compounded interest decrease the final death benefit, making the interest rate a key factor in determining the net payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="c0cc74e7-542a-4528-ba0d-09bdfde98f5d">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that outstanding loans and accrued interest be deducted from the death benefit implies that failing to pay interest results in higher future liabilities, reinforcing the importance of timely interest payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="9385aac2-9570-4e2e-8922-87d7cad0451d">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit is diminished by outstanding loans and accumulated interest, potentially leading to a situation where liabilities exceed the cash value, triggering policy termination.</data>
      <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="d5989a8e-5059-4901-af97-50fb73edccc0">
      <data key="d3">The deduction of outstanding loans and accrued interest from the death benefit necessitates that such interest be tracked and compounded over time, reinforcing the need to account for interest being added to the loan balance.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces benefit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="6025efda-5892-4057-8c1a-24a08309d3ef">
      <data key="d3">When loans remain unpaid, they diminish the death benefit by subtracting accumulated debt and interest. This reduction directly affects what beneficiaries receive upon the insured's passing.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that loans and interest reduce the death benefit, which directly supports the operational detail in fact_sentence_2 about how insurers calculate payouts using those deductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="62ce7dc7-8d45-41ca-8622-42a08799f32e">
      <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit by outstanding loans and interest implies that borrowers must have previously accessed the cash value through a loan, which requires the policy to be active for at least one year.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="528ac7df-43ef-4675-962b-37d25d763e12">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to deduct outstanding loans and accrued interest from the death benefit necessitates an understanding of how interest accumulates—specifically through annual compounding.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="c480fe05-ce9f-4a3f-850c-78f45358c91e">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans drawn against the cash surrender value diminish the net proceeds available upon surrender, thereby reducing the actual cash surrender value received.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces value</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="420a5002-0682-40c2-84f4-05f7e8ef1e48">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce both the death benefit and cash surrender value, thereby diminishing the pool of funds that could otherwise support future dividend accumulation or increase paid-up additions over time.</data>
      <data key="d4">reduces base</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="44d166e8-5546-4afd-be9d-b8fb4e61a5df">
      <data key="d3">The reduction of the death benefit by outstanding loans and interest depends on the availability of policy loans backed by cash value, as enabled by the policy’s terms.</data>
      <data key="d4">result of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, so if a policyholder opts for paid-up insurance due to unpaid debts, the resulting benefit reflects those reductions.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="a7e90d89-0d41-4335-b810-2d09e0514f0f" target="e4e45c14-e67b-4e30-b13b-2739562070cd">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is reduced by</data>
    </edge>
