    <edge source="0e45bbad-ae20-4562-bed9-67e55a13cadc" target="84a7b196-2336-4dd5-8ec6-5834754c1add">
      <data key="d3">The death benefit computation depends on accumulated elements like paid-up additions, which themselves can grow through dividend allocations mentioned in the first statement. Thus, the presence of extra cash value via dividends indirectly supports larger paid-up additions used in determining the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">enhances</data>
