      <data key="d3">The death benefit is reduced by any outstanding policy loans and accumulated interest, meaning that higher loan usage—up to 90% of the cash surrender value—directly diminishes what beneficiaries receive. Thus, the loan limit defines the upper bound of potential reductions in the final payout.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
