    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes one of several non-forfeiture options available upon stopping premiums after three years—the right to receive a cash surrender value. This option is presented alongside other alternatives like reduced paid-up insurance, making it part of a set of equal-choice provisions.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after three years, the policyholder may select the CASH SURRENDER option, which enables them to receive the accumulated cash value and end the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">Cash surrender offers immediate liquidity by paying out the policy's cash value, while reduced paid-up insurance continues coverage with a smaller death benefit without requiring more premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after three years, the policyholder can select either cash surrender or extended term insurance as alternative outcomes. The existence of one does not affect the other’s validity—both are viable choices under identical conditions.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">Cash surrender provides immediate liquidity by paying out the accumulated cash value, while extended term insurance uses that same cash value to extend life insurance protection without additional premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder stops paying premiums after three years and chooses cash surrender, they forfeit other options. If no decision is made within 60 days, the system defaults to extended term insurance instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">defaults to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder stops paying premiums after three years, they may select extended term insurance as a non-forfeiture benefit. Under this option, no additional premiums are required because coverage continues using the accumulated cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that cash surrender is available after three years of premium payments, directly relying on the defined meaning of Cash Surrender Value explained in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Cash surrender gives a lump sum upon stopping premiums, whereas paid-up insurance maintains a lower death benefit indefinitely. These represent different paths for handling unused policy value.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary options</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="14831871-1bdc-4e03-8d4e-447669d9085a" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">time constraint for</data>
    </edge>
