    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines another non-forfeiture choice available under identical conditions: converting the policy into a reduced paid-up insurance plan without further premium payments. It stands as an equivalent alternative to cash surrender, not dependent on or derived from it.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance maintains life insurance protection without additional premiums, serving as an alternative to Cash Surrender, which terminates coverage entirely and pays out the cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 outlines the availability of Reduced Paid-Up Insurance as an option upon stopping premiums after three years. Fact sentence 2 adds that Extended Term Insurance is also available under the same conditions, offering a different method to retain life insurance protection without further premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after three years, the policyholder may select Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, which ensures ongoing life insurance protection without requiring future payments, albeit at a diminished death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance provides a smaller permanent coverage amount without further premium payments. This contrasts with Extended Term Insurance, which uses accumulated cash value to maintain the original face amount for a time-limited duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder stops paying premiums after three years, they may select Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, which is part of the broader set of non-forfeiture options including Extended Term Insurance, where no future premiums are needed.</data>
      <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4">
      <data key="d3">When premiums cease after three years, the policyholder may select Reduced Paid-Up Insurance. The specific amount of this coverage depends on the accumulated cash value and the insured's current age at the time of election.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder fails to act on reducing paid-up insurance after premium cessation, the insurer defaults to providing extended term coverage instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">defaults to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the conditions under which Reduced Paid-Up Insurance applies, confirming that it is a viable outcome when premiums end after three years—a scenario consistent with the definition provided in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Non-Forfeiture Option Reduced Paid-Up Insurance relies on the policy's cash value, making the calculation of Cash Surrender Value essential to understanding its implementation and limitations.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="716dbb6e-443c-4a3d-b420-b92a8a31ab1e" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
