    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="4efbedc6-1cfd-4358-ac83-80bd56506e46">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, mentioned in fact_sentence_2, represents a potential consequence of ceasing premium payments, aligning with the scenario implied in fact_sentence_1 where policies may transition into non-active states affecting final payouts.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="5ea73efa-2572-4665-a567-0bc08cfeff08">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance offers a permanent, low-cost death benefit option that aligns with streamlined claim processes by eliminating future premiums while still enabling swift disbursement upon proof of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance ensures ongoing protection with diminished benefits, whereas cash surrender terminates the policy and returns its accumulated value.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance uses the policy’s cash value to maintain minimal coverage indefinitely without new premiums, ensuring residual protection. Cash Surrender liquidates that value completely by canceling the policy and returning funds to the holder.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance offers permanent coverage with no further premiums, making it an ideal choice when a policyholder stops paying premiums after three years and seeks to retain some level of protection.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance ensures ongoing coverage without additional premiums, while its specific death benefit amount depends on the accumulated cash value and the insured’s current age at conversion.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance offers ongoing coverage at a lower benefit level without future premium payments. This alternative becomes relevant only if elected before the lapse period ends, otherwise Extended Term Insurance defaults.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance offers permanent coverage without additional premiums but at a lower death benefit. This contrasts with Extended Term Insurance, another non-forfeiture choice allowing temporary coverage using accumulated cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance maintains coverage at a lower death benefit indefinitely without further premiums, whereas Extended Term Insurance uses cash value to provide full face amount protection for a time-limited period.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="b3ac5002-b47d-45fd-8c6f-813289686f71">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance offers ongoing coverage without future premiums, serving as a standalone solution after lapse. This contrasts with reinstatement, which requires proving insurability and paying overdue amounts.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance maintains coverage with a lower death benefit and no ongoing premiums. This contrasts with Extended Term Insurance, which also requires no further premiums but provides time-limited coverage instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">comparable to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance offers ongoing protection without further premiums, whereas reinstatement demands payment of delinquent amounts plus interest to restore the policy’s original status.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that reduced paid-up insurance maintains coverage indefinitely at a lower benefit level without requiring more payments, reinforcing the definition provided in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance enables continued protection without additional premiums, whereas Cash Surrender Value represents the liquidated return if the policy is terminated early. One preserves coverage; the other ends it for monetary gain.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5c8750ad-4a15-4dfa-91e6-2b52de2030a5" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
