    <edge source="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance uses the available cash value and the insured’s current age to determine its benefit level, reflecting an outcome tied to the financial value released under cash surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">informs</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">The availability of Reduced Paid-Up Insurance as a non-forfeiture choice hinges on having maintained the policy for at least three years. Its value is calculated using the policy’s cash value and the insured’s attained age.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">The amount of Reduced Paid-Up Insurance is calculated using the cash value and the insured’s attained age, directly determining the level of continued coverage received under the plan.</data>
      <data key="d4">determines</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance depends on cash value and age, offering a permanent benefit without further payments. Extended term insurance provides temporary coverage equal to the original sum assured, also triggered by stopping premiums after three years.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">Reduced Paid-Up Insurance determines its benefit level using the cash value and the insured’s current age, offering permanent coverage at a lower face amount. This contrasts with Extended Term Insurance, which leverages the same cash value to provide temporary coverage equal to the original face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4" target="fdebe47d-6d0f-4dce-a65b-cbc219fc28d4">
      <data key="d3">Reduced paid-up insurance is calculated using the insured’s current cash value and attained age. When age is misrepresented, the benefit is recalculated to reflect what the original premiums would have bought at the accurate age, maintaining fairness in coverage despite initial error.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.92</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="832dd780-4994-4375-8f15-00e86447e70d" target="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">increases cash value</data>
    </edge>
