    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">The availability of extended term insurance upon premium cessation after three years implies that cash surrender is also an eligible choice, reflecting multiple non-forfeiture pathways offered simultaneously under the same scenario.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance offers continued protection using the policy’s cash value, serving as an alternative to Cash Surrender, which terminates coverage entirely and pays out the cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 identifies Extended Term Insurance as a viable choice when premiums cease after three years. Fact sentence 1 complements this by specifying that Reduced Paid-Up Insurance is another eligible option under identical circumstances, illustrating complementary alternatives.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance enables continuation of coverage for a limited period without paying more premiums. It serves as an alternate non-forfeiture option compared to Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, which maintains lifelong protection at a smaller benefit level.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4">
      <data key="d3">When premiums stop after three years, the policyholder can select extended term insurance as a non-forfeiture option. The amount of reduced paid-up insurance is calculated from the current cash value and the insured's age at that time.</data>
      <data key="d4">related to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">When premiums are stopped after three years, the policyholder may select Extended Term Insurance as a non-forfeiture option. This option uses the accumulated cash value to provide coverage equal to the original face amount for a specified duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">explains</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder stops paying premiums after three years, they may select Extended Term Insurance as an option. Under this choice, no additional premiums are required, allowing coverage to continue temporarily without cost.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">When a policyholder fails to make premium payments after three years, they have the right to select Extended Term Insurance. If no selection is made within 60 days, the system defaults to applying Extended Term Insurance automatically.</data>
      <data key="d4">defaults to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="fdebe47d-6d0f-4dce-a65b-cbc219fc28d4">
      <data key="d3">When premiums stop after three years, the policyholder may select extended term insurance. However, if the original age was wrong, the resulting coverage is adjusted so it reflects what could have been bought at the true age.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance provides continued coverage after premium stops, whereas Cash Surrender Value represents the monetary return upon withdrawal; these represent opposing but related choices at policy termination, with one preserving benefit and the other liquidating value.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative outcome</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance enables continued protection beyond the premium period by leveraging saved cash value, whereas paid-up insurance maintains a lower fixed death benefit permanently. They represent different strategies for preserving coverage upon ceasing premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="eb6ae5af-a747-4319-af9e-554b7c596bf6" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">determines coverage level in extended term insurance</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="8f7ae7bd-6fb9-45a9-8272-6281a9b8d284" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is eligible upon stopping premiums after 3 years</data>
    </edge>
