      <data key="d4">exclusion</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="1a6eb5f8-54c3-40ab-9b5b-2c883102b417">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">exclusion</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="3f67c86f-51bd-4044-966e-a6b3ff26e74f">
      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">period</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance offers continued coverage equivalent to the original face amount using remaining cash value, whereas cash surrender terminates the policy and pays out the net cash value directly.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance utilizes the accumulated cash value to maintain life insurance protection without further premium payments, offering an alternative to cash surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance offers temporary life coverage equal to the original face amount by leveraging the policy's cash value. It serves as an alternative to Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, which reduces the coverage permanently while eliminating future premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance extends the full face amount for a set time using cash value, contrasting with Reduced Paid-Up Insurance that reduces the death benefit but ensures permanent coverage without more payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="8b98c6ac-7eb3-4170-b9c4-eba31a5b67b4">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance provides a time-bound continuation of the full face amount by utilizing available cash value. In contrast, Reduced Paid-Up Insurance offers permanent but diminished coverage determined by the same cash value and the insured’s attained age.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance maintains the full face amount of the policy for a limited period by utilizing the policy's cash value, serving as one of the non-forfeiture options available if premiums are discontinued after three years.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance uses accumulated cash value to maintain coverage without requiring new premiums, ensuring continued protection at the original face amount.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance provides continued coverage at the full face amount using available cash value. If no choice is made within 60 days post-lapse, this option activates automatically.</data>
      <data key="d4">automates</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="fdebe47d-6d0f-4dce-a65b-cbc219fc28d4">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance provides temporary coverage using accumulated cash value, but its face amount may be revised downward if the original age was inaccurately stated, ensuring alignment with actuarial expectations at the true age.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance depends on the residual cash value after deducting loans and fees, making it reliant on the precise calculation of cash surrender value.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance provides temporary full coverage using cash value, whereas paid-up insurance offers permanent reduced coverage without premiums, representing different outcomes from the same triggering event.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary options</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5a2b82b1-92a4-4694-926b-277eec59e747" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">is maintained</data>
    </edge>
