    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="4efbedc6-1cfd-4358-ac83-80bd56506e46">
      <data key="d3">The absence of further premium requirements under extended term insurance supports its use when settling a life insurance claim, aligning with how the final payout is determined based on policy options selected at time of death.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="5ea73efa-2572-4665-a567-0bc08cfeff08">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance eliminates the need for ongoing premiums, allowing timely access to benefits once a claim is validated and processed within the specified timeframe.</data>
      <data key="d4">precedes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">The absence of premium payments in extended term insurance reflects its nature as a non-forfeiture option chosen by policyholders who have ceased paying premiums after three years, allowing continued protection without ongoing costs.</data>
      <data key="d4">caused by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance provides continued protection at no cost after premium payment stops, whereas Cash Surrender fully ends the policy and delivers a lump sum instead.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance, like Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, is a non-forfeiture option available upon cessation of premium payments after three years, ensuring coverage continues without ongoing payment obligations.</data>
      <data key="d4">part of</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance ensures temporary coverage without requiring more premiums, similar to how Reduced Paid-Up Insurance sustains protection at a diminished level indefinitely.</data>
      <data key="d4">comparable to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">The absence of further premium requirements defines Extended Term Insurance, making it a viable non-forfeiture option when premiums cease after three years of policy duration.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">The absence of premium requirements enables extended term insurance to sustain coverage for a set duration using available cash value, preserving the full face amount during that time.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance activates automatically when no election is made within 60 days of lapse, eliminating the need for future premiums.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="fdebe47d-6d0f-4dce-a65b-cbc219fc28d4">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance provides coverage without additional premiums, but its face amount may be revised if the original age information was inaccurate, ensuring alignment with actuarial expectations.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance depends on having enough cash value available, making it reliant on the calculation defined by the cash surrender value formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance enables coverage continuation without further premiums, mirroring the core feature described in paid-up insurance—elimination of premium obligation while preserving a death benefit.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="fd85582c-5243-445d-98d8-8b5a9ab69f30" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">available within 3 years of lapse</data>
    </edge>
