    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="9054f79e-c024-42c1-ab31-f6a85012ac7b">
      <data key="d3">The absence of a chosen non-forfeiture option like cash surrender triggers automatic enrollment in extended term insurance after 60 days, ensuring coverage continuity without active selection.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers fallback</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance applies automatically if no decision is made within 60 days of lapse, serving as a fallback. This contrasts with cash surrender, which requires explicit selection to end the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">default after</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="b13a632f-d54c-467f-9a7f-83f5e5c712e6">
      <data key="d3">The application of extended term insurance serves as a fallback mechanism when the policyholder does not select alternative non-forfeiture options like reduced paid-up insurance.</data>
      <data key="d4">fallback for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance activates automatically if no election is made within 60 days of lapse, serving as a fallback option. It contrasts with Reduced Paid-Up Insurance, which requires active selection instead of relying on default rules.</data>
      <data key="d4">defaults to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="63ff27ef-e3e0-4f42-bbe9-ee3129a67647">
      <data key="d3">The automatic application of Extended Term Insurance upon failure to act within 60 days serves as a fallback mechanism ensuring coverage continuity when the policyholder does not exercise their option to choose it voluntarily.</data>
      <data key="d4">fallback for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="10bf0615-4e53-4ca9-9f8f-24f248922077">
      <data key="d3">When no decision is made within 60 days after a policy lapses, Extended Term Insurance becomes effective. This ensures the continuation of the full face amount for a duration tied to the policy’s cash value.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="d9857520-5a18-4a32-8752-3f61f66f696a">
      <data key="d3">The automatic application of extended term insurance upon lapse ensures coverage continues without requiring any further premium payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="fdebe47d-6d0f-4dce-a65b-cbc219fc28d4">
      <data key="d3">When no action is taken within 60 days of lapse, Extended Term Insurance activates automatically. In cases where the insured’s age was inaccurately reported, EFIT recalculates the face amount to reflect coverage that could have been obtained at the true age.</data>
      <data key="d4">causes adjustment</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="4871bb62-321f-47dd-8890-1d5bf5de7bcf">
      <data key="d3">When a policy lapses and no election is made within 60 days, Extended Term Insurance (EFIT) activates automatically. In such cases, if the insured dies by suicide within two years, EFIT pays only the total premiums paid, excluding interest.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions efit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Extended Term Insurance serves as a non-cash alternative to cash surrender, making the calculation of Cash Surrender Value less relevant if this option is selected by default.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Extended term insurance acts as a fallback option when no choice is made after a lapse, whereas paid-up insurance is a deliberate selection offering lifelong protection at a lower benefit level.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary option</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="9a0fe31a-f55b-419f-83a4-ab352fb268d7" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
