    <edge source="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4" target="0c1d3d36-ecf7-4afe-973c-5c905fcb9ec8">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves paying back missed premiums with interest, unlike reduced paid-up insurance, which permanently reduces the death benefit without any new payments.</data>
      <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4" target="b3ac5002-b47d-45fd-8c6f-813289686f71">
      <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a policy hinges on proving insurability. However, even with acceptable health status, reinstatement cannot occur without settling all unpaid premiums and accrued interest at 6%.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4" target="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the need to pay overdue premiums with interest, which supports the overall requirement for reinstatement. This condition complements fact_sentence_2 by ensuring all financial liabilities tied to premium payments are settled before restoration.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest for reinstatement contrasts with the concept of paid-up insurance, which eliminates future payments entirely. While reinstatement restores original coverage, paid-up insurance provides a reduced but guaranteed benefit permanently.</data>
      <data key="d4">complementary to</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves repaying delinquent payments with interest, which affects the available cash surrender value upon future surrender, showing that reinstated policies may have altered surrender terms due to accumulated debt.</data>
      <data key="d4">influences</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="731fe145-d64f-47d4-a8fe-ee687b5ec726" target="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">subject to payment during reinstatement</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e862cceb-d726-497c-a150-4b0112c7901c" target="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4">
      <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
      <data key="d4">reinstatement window</data>
    </edge>
