    </edge>
    <edge source="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff" target="747cc78d-f00a-40a8-979b-9890c223d923">
      <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy necessitates paying off loans with interest, meaning that choosing cash surrender would eliminate eligibility for reinstatement unless the loan was already settled before surrender.</data>
      <data key="d4">prevents</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff" target="b3ac5002-b47d-45fd-8c6f-813289686f71">
      <data key="d3">The requirement to repay policy loans with interest ensures that reinstatement remains financially viable and aligns with the conditions set for proving insurability during reinstatement.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff" target="777d5357-97c8-4051-86e0-1ca68438a2f4">
      <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that unpaid policy loans must also be repaid with interest during reinstatement. This directly relates to fact_sentence_1, as both involve fulfilling monetary obligations involving interest to restore policy validity.</data>
      <data key="d4">complements</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff" target="310584c0-76a7-4455-8d4e-410439b625ea">
      <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires paying off existing loans with interest, which contradicts the premise of paid-up insurance—where such debts would typically need resolution before conversion, making reinvestment moot afterward.</data>
      <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff" target="07e5a874-62e0-4196-a2d8-9165fd8a7041">
      <data key="d3">Reinstatement necessitates paying back loans with interest, reinforcing the importance of loan balances in determining the net value available upon surrender, as defined by the Cash Surrender Value formula.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="578cae3b-65b0-4354-b558-df7eba876c53" target="1aca0368-1bec-44f3-997c-933cfa6b6cff">
