    <edge source="4871bb62-321f-47dd-8890-1d5bf5de7bcf" target="4efbedc6-1cfd-4358-ac83-80bd56506e46">
      <data key="d3">Suicide within two years triggers a limitation on the death benefit, overriding the standard formula that includes face amount and additions.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4871bb62-321f-47dd-8890-1d5bf5de7bcf" target="5ea73efa-2572-4665-a567-0bc08cfeff08">
      <data key="d3">The restriction that suicide within two years reduces payout to premiums paid applies regardless of the standard seven-day processing timeline for claims.</data>
      <data key="d4">modifies</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="4871bb62-321f-47dd-8890-1d5bf5de7bcf" target="f96958f0-bbcb-476e-be0c-004fac2bd620">
      <data key="d3">The rule limiting EFIT payouts to premiums paid (without interest) in case of suicide within two years applies specifically when EFIT has been activated due to a lapse and lack of an election. This outcome depends on EFIT's automatic implementation per the prior clause.</data>
      <data key="d4">triggers efit</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="6b25adfa-b125-46f1-8dd8-0defc65f2597" target="4871bb62-321f-47dd-8890-1d5bf5de7bcf">
