    <edge source="df7e92d9-343b-4b72-82e8-0f1fcae86bd2" target="c580619d-07d0-45d8-b554-365e608170c8">
      <data key="d3">Knowing the signature date allows determination of whether the policyholder is still within the 30-day window to cancel without penalty.</data>
      <data key="d4">enables</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df7e92d9-343b-4b72-82e8-0f1fcae86bd2" target="5c3810ca-e6ef-4d1e-8db1-8029eb2277f1">
      <data key="d3">The policy’s signature date sets the start point for determining eligibility under the contestability clause described in fact_sentence_2. Without knowing when the policy began, one cannot determine whether the insurer still holds rights to contest based on misrepresentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets context for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="df7e92d9-343b-4b72-82e8-0f1fcae86bd2" target="b2c34fb3-de6b-4d19-be40-3fdbc69743bb">
      <data key="d3">The policy's signature date on February 1, 2024, sets the effective date, initiating the two-year contestability period during which the insurer may challenge coverage due to misrepresentation.</data>
      <data key="d4">sets timing</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
