    <edge source="e3937ea4-ef37-43e5-bddb-1d3aabba2fb2" target="04d4a09c-1505-4f0e-9512-0c47ee4ef195">
      <data key="d3">The constraint that contestability only occurs while the insured is alive implies a need for a formally issued policy, such as one from Guardian Family Protection Corp., to exist before such rules apply.</data>
      <data key="d4">required for</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.65</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3937ea4-ef37-43e5-bddb-1d3aabba2fb2" target="5c3810ca-e6ef-4d1e-8db1-8029eb2277f1">
      <data key="d3">The requirement that the insurer can only contest coverage while the insured is alive limits the applicability of the grounds for contestation, such as material misrepresentation in the application.</data>
      <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="e3937ea4-ef37-43e5-bddb-1d3aabba2fb2" target="b2c34fb3-de6b-4d19-be40-3fdbc69743bb">
      <data key="d3">For the insurer to exercise its contestability rights, the policy must be within the first two years, and the insured must remain alive during that period.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
