      <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
      <data key="d4">date</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5c3810ca-e6ef-4d1e-8db1-8029eb2277f1" target="04d4a09c-1505-4f0e-9512-0c47ee4ef195">
      <data key="d3">The restriction allowing the insurer to contest coverage only due to material misrepresentation applies specifically to Guardian Family Protection Corp., the entity that issued the policy.</data>
      <data key="d4">limits</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.85</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5c3810ca-e6ef-4d1e-8db1-8029eb2277f1" target="df7e92d9-343b-4b72-82e8-0f1fcae86bd2">
      <data key="d3">The existence of a contestability period tied to material misrepresentation depends on the policy being active; thus, its relevance hinges on the policy having been signed, as indicated by the signature date in fact_sentence_1.</data>
      <data key="d4">depends on timing</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.75</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5c3810ca-e6ef-4d1e-8db1-8029eb2277f1" target="b2c34fb3-de6b-4d19-be40-3fdbc69743bb">
      <data key="d3">The second sentence defines the grounds for contestability—material misrepresentation—and the first limits those grounds to apply only within the first two years after the policy's start.</data>
      <data key="d4">limited by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="5c3810ca-e6ef-4d1e-8db1-8029eb2277f1" target="e3937ea4-ef37-43e5-bddb-1d3aabba2fb2">
      <data key="d3">Material misrepresentation serves as the sole justification for contesting a policy, but this right is restricted to cases where the insured is still alive at the time of challenge.</data>
      <data key="d4">justified by</data>
      <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
      <data key="d5">0.95</data>
    </edge>
